  "script": "OpenAI just answered the AI model race. One week after Anthropic released Claude Fable 5.2, OpenAI launched GPT-6.2 Astra and GPT-6.2 Sol. Astra is built for demanding professional work: documents, slides, code, and even frontends for websites, games, and 3D design. Sol is the faster everyday model, made to handle more tasks on the same paid plan. The pricing is the headline. Astra costs eight dollars per million input tokens and forty for output. Sol costs two dollars in and ten dollars out. OpenAI says Astra sets a new quality bar for complex work at a much lower price than before. The frontier isn’t just smarter. It’s getting cheaper and faster.",
